{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1114845-skin-dancers-and-rites","id":1114845,"title":"Skin Dancers and Rites?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-11T18:30:57-07:00","id":1114845,"title":"Skin Dancers and Rites?","content":"I understand that Skin Dancers do not have an easy time learning Gifts, but what about performing Rites? If a Skin Dancer, particularly one who received his pelts from a willing donor who had access to someone with super regeneration capabilities, learned Gaian Rites would that Skin Dancer be able to perform the Rite?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T20:05:35-07:00","id":1114875,"title":"","content":"The Rite says &quot;If successful, the preserved, stitched hides of the slain Garou meld onto the ritemaster's body&quot; and &quot;Unless the Garou who were slain by the ritemaster gave their lives to him willingly, the Wyrm will grievously taint the ritemaster&quot;. You have to kill five Garou to become a Garou, you cannot just skin five willing Garou to avoid the Wyrm taint, you have to kill five willing Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T05:52:24-07:00","id":1115052,"title":"","content":"Per the system, Aya is correct, it states that the skin donor must be slain. To clarify, you don't need special regeneration to survive a live skinning. The Get of Fenris have a fetish that it created by skinning themselves and then turning the husk into a literal second skin. <br /> <br /> As for if Skin Dancer's can use rites, all they need are spirits willing to power the rite. So, imo, rites that a thematically appropriate for Minotaur might be possible for the Skin Dancer's. Really its a call of the storyteller. Given the ritual nature of their birth I tend to have them use more hedge magic then spiritual rites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T12:31:35-07:00","id":1115191,"title":"","content":"Ok, thanks all for the info. I guess I just had that old White Wolf book Hell Storm stuck in my head where one of the BSDs Haight skinned just barely survived and eventually healed and chased after... um... The last White Howler. In retrospect maybe I should be mindful the novels aren't really canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T12:40:17-07:00","id":1115196,"title":"","content":"I remember the story as well and you are right, he does skin the BSD alive, but we never actually see the skin get used for the Rite either. There is a good chance that even though he harvested it, because the BSD survived it wasn't usable for the rite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T12:55:07-07:00","id":1115206,"title":"","content":"I wonder if it counts if the Changer dies but is then brought back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T14:28:21-07:00","id":1115256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1114845-skin-dancers-and-rites?p=1115206#post1115206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if it counts if the Changer dies but is then brought back.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could make for an interesting story line where the skin dancers permanency is threatened. Could be that because their essence was used in a such a way that they are unable to be brought back. Kind of like that new BSD gift that steals the soul. There aren't many ways to bring them back from the dead though so its kind of unlikely but might make for a cruel story line.<br /> <br /> Pack goes on a long quest to bring a fallen hero back from the dead only to find out that they can't because his soul is the glue holding another person together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T15:01:00-07:00","id":1115269,"title":"","content":"Cruel? I see it as a comedy, not a tragedy. The Skin Dancers should not be, W20 says so in the description of the Rite, so them getting their just deserts is a positive thing.<br /> <br /> I do not think that there is a single pack in the Ahadi, Beast Courts, or Garou Nation that would hesitate for a second to bring back a Garou if it meant that a Skin Dancer would lose their powers. Heck, I think that every Garou in those organizations would think that it was a bonus and would be trying to use the same method to bring the other four slain Garou back to life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T15:34:33-07:00","id":1115277,"title":"","content":"Aya you aren't understanding what I am saying. The cruel part is that the pack would be doomed to fail at first because the fallen warriors soul is partially bound to the skin dancer. The pack wouldn't know that though until they got to the end of their first quest.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T18:34:45-07:00","id":1115322,"title":"","content":"Well, it would just give another reason for them to eliminate a Skin Dancer (like they need any more reason than that they murdered five Garou).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T19:10:45-07:00","id":1115337,"title":"","content":"We get it, you don't like Skin Dancers. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But yeah, that would be Act II.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T20:48:49-07:00","id":1115360,"title":"","content":"What I do not understand is why anyone would like them? What is admirable about a murderer who betrays everything for their own personal gain?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T05:52:10-07:00","id":1115492,"title":"","content":"Its because you are looking at them through a very small lens. Its the same appeal of Kithian or Ghouls. They are the little guy who gets power and then runs with it. Also, if they kill only BSD to fuel the rite then technically they are fighting Gaia's fight. The only reason they are looked down upon is because they have started using the Wyrms tools against it. Its the Antihero/Vigilante appeal, like the Punisher or Venom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T07:32:00-07:00","id":1115519,"title":"","content":"What you are describing is the role of the Kinfolk who either learn Numina or Gifts, not the role of the Skin Dancers (I do not know if there really is an equivalent to the Skin Dancers in the other gamelines). Yes, there might be one special snowflake Skin Dancer who was created from the skins of Black Spiral Dancers, but the existence of one 'good' Skin Dancer does not justify the other 99 'evil' Skin Dancers (anyway, the fact that they sought out the Skin Dancers and/or agents of the Wyrm for the Rite suggests that they were probably never intending to go after Black Spiral Dancers). Every other Skin Dancer was created by killing and skinning their own flesh and blood, and there are probably nine failed Skin Dancers for every successful Skin Dancer since the Rite requires five skins from slain Garou (meaning that there are probably an average of 30 murdered and skinned Garou for every successful Skin Dancer and nine failed Skin Dancers). With the exception of one special snowflake Skin Dancer, every Skin Dancer who exists became Garou by murdering and skinning five Garou who trusted their Kinfolk and did not use the Wyrm's tools against the Wyrm, they did the job of the Wyrm by depriving Gaia of five warriors during her time of need so they could be a furry superhero. If people want to play evil Garou, they should go ahead and play Skin Dancers or Black Spiral Dancers if they want, but it is just as disingenuous to say that the Skin Dancers are the plucky Kinfolk resisting Garou tyranny as it is to say that Black Spiral Dancers are just misunderstood champions of freedom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T08:31:43-07:00","id":1115539,"title":"","content":"Skin Dancers are Kinfolk that learn Numina and Gifts, then they go one step farther so that they can fight them on equal footing. The other tribes have killed each other over territory, kin, fetishes, ideology, etc etc. They have raped and pillaged across the pure lands tribes to the point that the 2 remaining three brothers tribes are so close to falling to the Wyrm. They hunted the Bunyip to extinction. Most of the legitimate tribes are just as evil as the Skin Dancers they just are more acceptable because they do in the name of Gaia and plead ignorance after the fact.<br /> <br /> As I said in a previous thread where you pretty much said the same thing, if you want them to be the boogeyman then run with it. I respect the choice and understand why you want that. That isn't what everyone believes about them. Some like to use them in a different way and that is what the OP was asking about. Potential alternative ideas. That is all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T10:21:24-07:00","id":1115575,"title":"","content":"Skindancers were, from their very beginning, npot meant to play a hero role but for ONE exception: 5 Garou of same auspiece dying willingly to empower one deserving Kinfolk. There are basically 2 types:<br /> <br /> The one that stole his empowerment. No matter if he slew BSD or Garou Nation Garou, he stole the gifts of Gaia and the spirit world by force. The BSD slayer might be somewhat forgiven, but his soul is of the wyrm for two reasons: the rite that made him is of the wyrm, and the souls bound in the pelts he used did dance the spiral. Because of that, his very soul is heavily tainted. Even though his creation brought the death of BSD and he might fight them, this taint he can't wash away. He is the involuntary villain amomg villains that hunt Garou Nation Garou for more SkinDancers. The Nation will smell his taint (unless he gets a powerful gift to hide it) and slay him as a BSD.<br /> <br /> The one that got the 5 pelts gifted. He is the one special snowflake that didn't steal his way to power, but he was gifted it. His rite is not tainted for it was gifted. He is... the very very special snowflake, he is the one in a million. Still, his existance deprived Gaia of 5 Garou, probably old ones that were wise but too old to fight. He is the only exception, the tragic hero with the dark past, 5 anchestors (that gave their life for him!) loom over his shoulder and demand him to live up to ALL their legacies. And because he is still weak in the beginning, he is doomed to fail several times.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> System wise: nothing prevents a SkinDancer from learning Rites but having to find a teacher. Usually teachers are Garou, in rare cases the totems and anchestors, in very rare cases it is an Incarna itself teaching.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9729-hira-akigi","name":"Hira Akigi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T01:05:51-07:00","id":1115837,"title":"","content":"Honestly Skindancers work best for a legitimate redemption arc. The whole &quot;just die/Go directly to Erebus do not past go&quot; really doesn't help. This someone who's hubris has looked into the Face of God and said &quot;You made a mistake. You should have picked me!&quot; The process they have going forward past now that they have to deal with &quot;what the hell have I done&quot; works as great storytelling potential, especially when you have the &quot;Good&quot; skindancer who got all his kills from BSDs! When he learns even that is of the wyrm. <br /> <br /> And then there's the bigger question. Why is there a nontainted option? If this is a purely of the wyrm how could there be a nontainted Option? It can't be to lure people in because there's no way they'd possibly know this. If its not from the Wyrm then what does it mean?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T09:06:55-07:00","id":1115970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1114845-skin-dancers-and-rites#post1114845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Skin Dancer, particularly one who received his pelts from a willing donor who had access to someone with super regeneration capabilities, learned Gaian Rites would that Skin Dancer be able to perform the Rite?</div> </div> </div> </div>Skin Dancers are tainted by the Wyrm. It's an end story, stop and do not pass Go situation. In your own games you can do what you want, but according to WW all Skin Dancers are Wyrm tainted. As such you have to deal with learning Gifts/Rites from those who will teach you. So can you find a Garou, a Spirit, or a Totem that serves Gaia who is willing to teach you if you are Wyrm tainted? 99.9% of the time no. Exceptions would be plot device the ST decided to include.<br /> <br /> Servants of Minotaur, Tick, or any aspect of Wyrm are likely the only options for teachers.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4579-skeleton-jack","name":"Skeleton Jack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T10:46:16-07:00","id":1116023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Skeleton Jack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1114845-skin-dancers-and-rites?p=1115970#post1115970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Servants of Minotaur, Tick, or any aspect of Wyrm are likely the only options for teachers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where does it say that Tick is a servant of the Wyrm? I don't remember any such thing being said in the Skinner SAS. In fact, I am pretty sure that part of Ticks plan was to legitimize the Tribe under her. The only way she could have done that was if she herself is considered a Gaian spirit. <br /> <br /> And where does it say that Minotaur has fallen? Minotaur serves himself, the book only states that he is Tainted by the Beast-of-War. Their is a difference in game terms both thematically and systematically on how Tainted and Fallen are handled. One of the endings of the Skinner SAS is Minotaur realizing that he has become tainted and upon realizing it starts to sound as if he might try to correct his mistakes. The possible outcome, again, being that that the tribe could potentially become legitimate. Bad blood with certain tribes withstanding obviously. <br /> <br /> Also, minions of the Wyrm are not the only spirits that teach Skin Dancers. The totem description only says that Minotaur helps them find spirits to teach them gifts. There are spirits in Minotaurs maze that are not corrupted or tainted: Pain, Death, Decay, Disease, Rage. These spirits are not tied to any totem brood, don't really care about the material world, and are all thematically appropriate teachers for many gifts. Coercing Gaian spirits to teach you gifts is not unheard of, normal Garou do it all the time. The price is just higher for Skin Dancers like it is for Ronin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T14:36:10-07:00","id":1116116,"title":"","content":"So much argument over a group that probably only numbers one to two dozen individuals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T18:26:11-07:00","id":1116191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1114845-skin-dancers-and-rites?p=1116116#post1116116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So much argument over a group that probably only numbers one to two dozen individuals.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Like half a dozen vampire bloodlines, Mage crafts.. Mummies...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T03:46:58-07:00","id":1116317,"title":"","content":"Maybe some breed of Mummies but the Amenti had the potential to be quite numerous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T11:14:35-07:00","id":1116483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1114845-skin-dancers-and-rites?p=1116317#post1116317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe some breed of Mummies but the Amenti had the potential to be quite numerous.</div> </div> </div> </div>You also had a period where the most common type of mummy had 50 active members. YOu had a period where there were only 7 Salubri that were supposed to exist at all. Discussing a &quot;tribe&quot; that has maybe 24 members isn't particularly out there for these sorts of things..<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T06:36:38-07:00","id":1117173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1114845-skin-dancers-and-rites?p=1115337#post1115337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of the legitimate tribes are just as evil as the Skin Dancers they just are more acceptable because they do in the name of Gaia and plead ignorance after the fact.</div> </div> </div> </div>Skin dancers do their metamorphosis out of jealousy, pride or thirst for power; fighting werewolves as equals is just a bonus. Even if someone may delude himself with that idea, truth is that they tortured and murdered five warriors just to become one of them. The balance is not in favour of Gaia, and refusing their natural role is surely not Gaia's will either. In fact, the atrocity they create is so much that the stench of the Wyrm is firmly melded into their souls.<br /> <br /> Sure, some skin dancer may skin black spiral dancers and thin the enemy out, but that is probably going to bring the Wyrm taint into him even more, corrupting their mind and making them even more dangerous to the natural balance.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We get it, you don't like Skin Dancers. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>Well, skin dancers look really like Mary Sue-ish, if you think about it.<br /> I don't think I'll ever allow a skin dancer in the party, not in a Gaian campaign. Best use of skin dancers is to portray the horror and the depravity of the descent into the Wyrm, or as part of the Wyrm hordes.<br /> Untainted skin dancers, that received their pelt from willing Garous, are white flies even among the Mary Sues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T06:44:49-07:00","id":1117175,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I have to agree. Kinfolk are Kinfolk because Gaia decided that they were meant to be Kinfolk and were not meant to be Garou. For them to defy the will of Gaia to the degree that they are willing to murder five of Gaia's chosen to become one of the Garou is one of the ultimate blasphemies against Gaia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T06:57:18-07:00","id":1117178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1114845-skin-dancers-and-rites?p=1117175#post1117175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I have to agree. Kinfolk are Kinfolk because Gaia decided that they were meant to be Kinfolk and were not meant to be Garou. For them to defy the will of Gaia to the degree that they are willing to murder five of Gaia's chosen to become one of the Garou is one of the ultimate blasphemies against Gaia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, how does that make sense? What about the Apis who could dramatically increase the rate of fera births? Were they nudging Gaia to change her plan? From where I am sitting this looks like a matter of genuine luck or Gaia has limited resources and she is passing out what little she has to give.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T11:47:36-07:00","id":1117330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1114845-skin-dancers-and-rites?p=1117178#post1117178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, how does that make sense? What about the Apis who could dramatically increase the rate of fera births? Were they nudging Gaia to change her plan? From where I am sitting this looks like a matter of genuine luck or Gaia has limited resources and she is passing out what little she has to give.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right. It simply chance. A supernatural genetic lottery that they lost out on. If the rite defied Gaia's plan outright then why can skins be donated willingly at all? Why does the Rite not give taint to all who perform it? Because passing on the birthright does not violate Gaia's plan, taking it by force is what ultimately does them in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T11:48:47-07:00","id":1117332,"title":"","content":"That was part of the job and the authority that Gaia gave the Apis because Gaia gave the Apis to ability to choose worthy Kinfolk couples to have Fera children. There is nothing that says that Gaia gave Skin Dancers the job and authority to murder five of her warriors to fulfill their selfish dreams of becoming a superhuman. In the former, Gaia chose Fera to act as her agents when it came to Fera and Kinfolk reproduction. In the latter, Gaia has nothing to do with the abominable practice and the Skin Dancers are spitting in her eye by murdering and skinning her favored children before pissing in her flower bed by using a Wyrm Rite to become a Garou.<br /> <br /> The Skin Dancers are sort of like Buffalo Bill from <i>Silence of the Lambs</i> (though they are making a Garou suit instead of a woman suit). Would the character of Buffalo Bill been justified in murdering and skinning multiple women for the woman suit if there was some magical rite that would make the transformation work? No, not even if the resulting woman was really, really sorry that she murdered and skinned multiple women, because she still murdered and skinned multiple women.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T12:51:38-07:00","id":1117380,"title":"","content":"No one is saying that the Skin Dancers are justified, just that unnatural assistance for upping fera production might not be frowned upon by Gaia in her last seconds.<br /> <br /> Say for instance an Etherite got ahold of Pentex's data on fera biology and learned how to mass produce Garou and other Fera, possibly even recreating lost Fera. Would Gaia really be offended by the sincere effort on the part of the mage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 07-17-2017, 03:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T13:00:07-07:00","id":1117386,"title":"","content":"Yes, which would probably manifest in horrifying levels of Paradox because Gaia did not give them that authority or power. Of course, a Mage could potentially make a spirit quest to gain permission.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T15:04:27-07:00","id":1117461,"title":"","content":"I actually have to agree with Aya there... A member of the Children of Gaia tried to clone Thylacine in the hopes of resurrecting the Bunyip... He succeeded in recreating the physical part but the spiritual part was hollow. The Wyrm filled the space and now there are 3 angry Hollow Walkers roaming the Australian outback. The CoG was pure in his intentions but he didn't understand the spiritual part which ultimately caused his failure. You are more likely to end up with more Mockery Breeds going that path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T18:00:51-07:00","id":1117521,"title":"","content":"The Mockery Breeds were created by those who understood the spiritual aspects of the Fera. Don't forget how the Fera and even Englings were captured and vivisected to have the formula created.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T19:32:09-07:00","id":1117541,"title":"","content":"Yeah but look at those breeds. With the exception of the Yeren, they are all neutered in some way compared to full shifters. They had a better idea but they still don't have the full picture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T20:01:02-07:00","id":1117560,"title":"","content":"Even the Yeren are not a complete success. After all, they do not have any natural aggravated damage attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T07:25:53-07:00","id":1117718,"title":"","content":"You know, I never realized that when I read through it. After reading back through it, they don't have access to an animal form either. So it goes to show that none of their &quot;successes&quot; are actually complete.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T07:43:47-07:00","id":1117729,"title":"","content":"Well, now that the Bitten are a thing, I guess the Skin Dancers are going to fade away?<br /> <br /> But in any case, the skins in question don't have to BE of the same Auspice, they have to DIE and be skinned under it. <br /> <br /> I could see situations where volunteers could be found, much like organ donation. Especially after larger battles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T10:35:02-07:00","id":1117833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1114845-skin-dancers-and-rites?p=1117729#post1117729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, now that the Bitten are a thing, I guess the Skin Dancers are going to fade away?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure what this is, is that supposed to be something hinted at for a next edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T11:17:20-07:00","id":1117861,"title":"","content":"Yes, if there is such a thing as people becoming Garou through being bitten, I think it is just one more reason to boycott nWW and Paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T11:29:00-07:00","id":1117868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1114845-skin-dancers-and-rites?p=1117861#post1117861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, if there is such a thing as people becoming Garou through being bitten, I think it is just one more reason to boycott nWW and Paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just read the MET description. Basically the Garou finally got their hands on the Rite that the Ratkin use to create more of themselves. It always felt weird to me that several shifters have rites to create more of their kind by the the other shifters never tried to use something similar. Not sure if I am ready to boycott yet, really want to see what their ideas is fully fleshed out before I write it off. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1114845-skin-dancers-and-rites?p=1117729#post1117729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, now that the Bitten are a thing, I guess the Skin Dancers are going to fade away?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they would still exist. The Bite sounds like it has the possibility to kill the Kinfolk. The Skin Dancers are selfish, why risk it? Focus shifts from anger to survival. They take skins here and there as they kill of the BSD. They become tolerable instead of reviled. Who knows. My only hope is that if they use the Bitten they aren't full Garou, just beefed up kinfolk. Maybe they get to choose 1 additional form that they can turn into and they get access to a few more gifts and tricks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T12:46:05-07:00","id":1117892,"title":"","content":"And killing 5 BSD ain't risky?. I think I, being selfish, would go for the Bite...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T13:44:40-07:00","id":1117916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1114845-skin-dancers-and-rites?p=1117892#post1117892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And killing 5 BSD ain't risky?. I think I, being selfish, would go for the Bite...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if they become more tolerable to the other Tribes then they can be part of their battles with the BSD. Then, those that are already Garou can take their spoils of war after the fact. Slower then the bite but in the longer run, yeah, it would be safer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T13:49:47-07:00","id":1117920,"title":"","content":"The Birthing Plague is thematically appropriate for the Ratkin because Ratkin are associated with disease, it is not thematically appropriate for the Garou. It just seems to be another example of the LARP crowd trying to ruin the game for the TT crowd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T12:06:55-07:00","id":1133488,"title":"","content":"First of all, I apologize for writing, because English is not my native language.<br /> <br /> Now a question, Skin Dancers are fertile, have anything been mentioned about their children?<